# credit_amount
# Feature description: Credit amount reflects the loan size requested.
# Usefulness: Larger loan sizes might represent higher risk; small amounts may be more likely to be repaid and are less risky.

# repayment_risk_interaction
# Feature description: Cross-product of credit_to_income_ratio and risk_score to model the interaction between repayment burden and credit risk.
# Usefulness: Combines credit risk with repayment burden to strengthen its relevance for predicting credit approval directly.

# stability_interaction
# Feature description: Interaction term between age_to_job_ratio and residence_stability to assess combined workforce and geographic stability.
# Usefulness: Stability factors enhance the prediction of reliability and potential creditworthiness over the long term.

# residence_since
# Feature description: Time in years of residence at the current address.
# Usefulness: Long-term residence can indicate geographic and lifestyle stability, reducing perceived risk.

# savings_status_encoding
# Feature description: Numerical encoding of savings account status categories.
# Usefulness: Financial health captured through savings status provides key information on ability to manage repayment.

# zscore_duration
# Feature description: Z-score transformation of the duration feature to standardize it across applicants.
# Usefulness: Allows consistent assessment across varying repayment periods, contributing to repayment ability evaluation.

# stability_risk_ratio
# Feature description: Ratio of stability_interaction to repayment_risk_interaction.
# Usefulness: Encodes the balance between stability and repayment risk into a single variable. Higher ratios indicate greater stability relative to risk, enhancing interpretability.
df['stability_risk_ratio'] = df['stability_interaction'] / df['repayment_risk_interaction']
end

